            <ArticleTitle>[Combined analgetic drug treatment with ibuprofen after 3rd molar osteotomy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>442-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a placebo-controlled double-blind study using 3 x 400 mg ibuprofen during the surgical removal of impacted and dislocated third molars, a pain reduction of 64% (p = 0.05) as against the placebo control group could be demonstrated on the day of surgery and the first postoperative day. In view of the published results of a double-blind study on the reduction of cheek swelling using dexamethasone, the perioperative combination of 3 x 600 mg ibuprofen with 2 x 6 mg dexamethasone seems to be helpful in reliably preventing pain and swelling after dental surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
